# Context

## Background
Workstream 4 (the flagship) of plans/2026-11-09-upstream-alignment.md:
version stacks rebuilt on the fork's ACL model, plus sorting, bulk
ops, team switcher, and storage bar.

## Why This Way
- Generated-type fact that unlocked this: convex/_generated derives
  types LIVE from schema.ts and module sources, so new fields and new
  functions in EXISTING modules typecheck locally; only new modules
  need codegen (why the Mux sweeps remain design-only).
- Grants: copied forward AND backfilled reciprocally — the review
  proved a forward-only bridge dead-ends an admin who cuts a version
  of a restricted stack (videos.get FORBIDDEN on older versions).
- Share links repoint at markAsReady, never createVersion: repointing
  during upload stranded every share viewer on an uploading head for
  the whole upload. Links always resolve to the newest READY version.
- listVersions filters per-row ACL (restricted siblings' metadata
  must not leak to members without grants).
- Bulk budgets: Convex per-mutation limits (db calls ~4096, writes,
  scheduled jobs) are pre-checked worst-case BEFORE any deletion,
  with distinct coded errors; a batch under the version cap could
  otherwise die mid-transaction with the wrong message.
- Watch metering needed no new cap logic: trackerKey is the videoId,
  so version switches reset the machine; a test pins no
  double-billing and the playhead resets on switch.

## Gotchas
- shareLinks.videoId = current READY head (schema.ts comment); every
  future head-change path must repoint via the markAsReady planner.
- Title sort indexes are BYTE-ordered, not locale-ordered (the test
  suite pins apple-before-Banana).
- finalizeAbandonedUpload is guarded but has no caller until the Mux
  sweeps land (plans/2026-11-09-mux-sweeps-design.md).
- Known deferred follow-up: version-upload progress hides on
  navigation (upload continues; surface via the layout manager).

